# The Class C narrowing for cited public URLs, as a patch
#
# WHAT THIS IS. One line of .github/workflows/redaction-gate.yml, adding one
# alternative to the gate's shared allowance so that a UUID-shaped path
# segment inside an http(s) URL on an allowlisted published-source host stops
# reading as session identity. The reasoning, the measured population, the
# residual cost and the rejected alternatives are in
# docs/security/redaction-gate-uuid-narrowing.md.
#
# WHY IT IS A PATCH AND NOT AN EDIT. A workflow file is outside the engineer
# seat's writable surface, and the runner's token has no `workflows` scope, so
# a push carrying this hunk is refused by GitHub before review. It needs the
# owner or HQ to apply it.
#
# APPLY, from the repository root:
#   git apply docs/security/redaction-gate-uuid-narrowing.patch
#
# VERIFY, in this order, all three from the repository root:
#   node --test scripts/redaction-check.test.mjs
#   node scripts/redaction-check.mjs
#   node scripts/uuid-shape-census.mjs
#
# The suite asserts that this patch makes exactly the edit its cases
# exercise, so a patch edited by hand out of step with the tests fails the
# test named "the committed patch makes exactly the edit these tests
# exercise" rather than passing quietly.
#
# ROLL BACK:
#   git apply -R docs/security/redaction-gate-uuid-narrowing.patch
#
--- a/.github/workflows/redaction-gate.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/redaction-gate.yml
@@ -26,7 +26,7 @@ jobs:
             hits=$(grep -rInE "$pattern" . \
               --exclude-dir=.git --exclude-dir=node_modules --exclude-dir=.ursa \
               --exclude=redaction-gate.yml 2>/dev/null \
-              | grep -vE '/(home/runner|Users/<you>|home/<you>)/|projects/-Users-you-' || true)
+              | grep -vE '/(home/runner|Users/<you>|home/<you>)/|projects/-Users-you-|https?://finance\.biggo\.com/[A-Za-z0-9._~%/+-]*[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}' || true)
             if [ -n "$hits" ]; then
               echo "::error::$label"
               printf '%s\n' "$hits" | head -20
